{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | sed -n '1,270p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ast-walker\n     2\t  \"Direct AST interpreter for the Yin Abstract Machine on DaoStream v2.\n     3\t\n     4\t   A CESK machine over raw AST maps with a linked continuation, a ready queue\n     5\t   and a wait set. `step` and `run` execute already-loaded work only: program\n     6\t   input is observed above the VM by `yin.vm.stream-observer`, which hands\n     7\t   each batch to `vm-load-program` through `run-on-stream`. `eval` converts\n     8\t   its supplied AST, loads it, and runs it without draining any independently\n     9\t   queued program input. v1's evaluator was driven through its own\n    10\t   `:in-stream`; removing that coupling is what V7 changed, so this evaluator\n    11\t   is v1's kernel, not v1 unchanged.\n    12\t\n    13\t   The port's other changes below the evaluator survive: opaque cursors,\n    14\t   outcome maps, a supplied stream constructor, a registry value, and no\n    15\t   waiters — the one deletion inside this namespace is v1's transport-local\n    16\t   waiter registration in `park-and-call`, whose continuation now parks in the\n    17\t   polling wait set like every other blocked read until the response arrives\n    18\t   on the call-out stream.\n    19\t\n    20\t   There is no `macro-expand` branch here, exactly as in v1: this evaluator\n    21\t   runs macro-free programs.\"\n    22\t  (:require [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    23\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    24\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    25\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.telemetry :as telemetry]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(declare ast-walker-restore)\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t;; =============================================================================\n    34\t;; ASTWalkerVM Record\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t\n    37\t(defrecord ASTWalkerVM\n    38\t  [blocked?       ; boolean, true if blocked\n    39\t   bridge         ; explicit host-side FFI bridge state\n    40\t   halted?        ; boolean, true when active continuation has completed\n    41\t   k              ; reified continuation or nil\n    42\t   program        ; last loaded AST program\n    43\t   control        ; current AST node or nil\n    44\t   env            ; persistent lexical scope map\n    45\t   id-counter     ; integer counter for unique IDs\n    46\t   parked         ; parked continuations map\n    47\t   primitives     ; primitive operations map\n    48\t   modules        ; module registry value\n    49\t   make-stream    ; host-supplied stream constructor, or nil\n    50\t   call-capacity  ; declared capacity of the FFI pair\n    51\t   ready-queue    ; vector of runnable continuations\n    52\t   store          ; heap memory map\n    53\t   value          ; last computed value\n    54\t   wait-set       ; vector of continuations waiting on a transport\n    55\t   telemetry      ; optional telemetry config (always nil in this slice)\n    56\t   telemetry-step ; telemetry snapshot counter\n    57\t   telemetry-t    ; telemetry transaction counter\n    58\t   vm-model       ; telemetry model keyword\n    59\t   ])\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn- cesk-return\n    63\t  \"Create a new ASTWalkerVM with updated CESK fields in a single allocation.\n    64\t   Preserves blocked, store, and scheduler fields from vm.\n    65\t   Derives :halted? from the new CESK state.\"\n    66\t  [^ASTWalkerVM vm control env k val]\n    67\t  (let [blocked (:blocked? vm)]\n    68\t    (->ASTWalkerVM blocked\n    69\t                   (:bridge vm)\n    70\t                   (and (not blocked) (nil? control) (nil? k))\n    71\t                   k\n    72\t                   (:program vm)\n    73\t                   control\n    74\t                   env\n    75\t                   (:id-counter vm)\n    76\t                   (:parked vm)\n    77\t                   (:primitives vm)\n    78\t                   (:modules vm)\n    79\t                   (:make-stream vm)\n    80\t                   (:call-capacity vm)\n    81\t                   (:ready-queue vm)\n    82\t                   (:store vm)\n    83\t                   val\n    84\t                   (:wait-set vm)\n    85\t                   (:telemetry vm)\n    86\t                   (:telemetry-step vm)\n    87\t                   (:telemetry-t vm)\n    88\t                   (:vm-model vm))))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn- handle-primitive-result\n    92\t  \"Shared logic for handling the result of a primitive function application.\n    93\t   Handles effect dispatch and blocking via engine/handle-effect.\"\n    94\t  [state result k env]\n    95\t  (if (module/effect? result)\n    96\t    (let [{:keys [state value blocked?]}\n    97\t          (engine/handle-effect\n    98\t            state\n    99\t            result\n   100\t            {:restore-fn ast-walker-restore,\n   101\t             :park-entry-fns {:stream/put (fn [_s _e r]\n   102\t                                            {:k k,\n   103\t                                             :env env,\n   104\t                                             :reason :put,\n   105\t                                             :stream-id (:stream-id r),\n   106\t                                             :datom (:val result)}),\n   107\t                              :stream/next (fn [_s _e r]\n   108\t                                             {:k k,\n   109\t                                              :env env,\n   110\t                                              :reason :next,\n   111\t                                              :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref r),\n   112\t                                              :stream-id (:stream-id r)})}})]\n   113\t      (if blocked?\n   114\t        (assoc state\n   115\t               :control nil\n   116\t               :k nil\n   117\t               :halted? false)\n   118\t        (cesk-return state nil env k value)))\n   119\t    (cesk-return state nil env k result)))\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\t(defn- call-response-wait-entry\n   123\t  \"The polling wait entry for a sent call awaiting its correlated response.\"\n   124\t  [call-id next-k env]\n   125\t  {:k {:type :dao.stream.apply/eval-call,\n   126\t       :next next-k,\n   127\t       :env env,\n   128\t       :call-id call-id},\n   129\t   :env env,\n   130\t   :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key},\n   131\t   :reason :next,\n   132\t   :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key})\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t(defn- park-and-call\n   136\t  \"Park the continuation, emit the request, and wait for its response.\n   137\t\n   138\t   The pair is checked before `park-continuation` deliberately: the park runs\n   139\t   before the first stream touch, so an error raised later would strand a\n   140\t   continuation in `:parked` and consume an id counter.\n   141\t\n   142\t   The request is retained, never dropped. A `full` call-in leaves the\n   143\t   identical encoded request in the polling wait set, which retries it, and\n   144\t   the call starts waiting for its response only once the append has\n   145\t   succeeded. `closed`, `invalid-value` and `transport-error` fail the call\n   146\t   here and name their outcome.\"\n   147\t  [state op args k env]\n   148\t  (let [{:keys [call-in]} (ffi/require-call-pair! (:store state) op)\n   149\t        response-cont {:type :dao.stream.apply/eval-call, :next k, :env env}\n   150\t        parked (engine/park-continuation state {:k response-cont, :env env})\n   151\t        parked-id (get-in parked [:value :id])\n   152\t        request (apply2/request parked-id op (vec args))\n   153\t        result (apply2/put-request! call-in request)]\n   154\t    (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   155\t      :dao.stream/ok\n   156\t      (-> parked\n   157\t          (update :wait-set\n   158\t                  (fnil conj [])\n   159\t                  (call-response-wait-entry parked-id k env))\n   160\t          (telemetry/emit-snapshot :bridge {:bridge-op op})\n   161\t          (assoc :control nil\n   162\t                 :k nil\n   163\t                 :value :yin/blocked\n   164\t                 :blocked? true\n   165\t                 :halted? false))\n   166\t      :dao.stream/full\n   167\t      (-> parked\n   168\t          (update :wait-set\n   169\t                  (fnil conj [])\n   170\t                  {:k {:type :dao.stream.apply/request-sent,\n   171\t                       :parked-id parked-id,\n   172\t                       :next k,\n   173\t                       :env env,\n   174\t                       :op op},\n   175\t                   :env env,\n   176\t                   :reason :put,\n   177\t                   :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key,\n   178\t                   :datom request})\n   179\t          (telemetry/emit-snapshot :bridge {:bridge-op op})\n   180\t          (assoc :control nil\n   181\t                 :k nil\n   182\t                 :value :yin/blocked\n   183\t                 :blocked? true\n   184\t                 :halted? false))\n   185\t      (throw (ex-info \"FFI request could not be appended\"\n   186\t                      {:op op,\n   187\t                       :outcome (or (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   188\t                                    (:dao.stream.apply/outcome result))})))))\n   189\t\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn- call-result\n   192\t  \"Unwrap a response envelope for the continuation that made the call.\n   193\t\n   194\t   v1 read `:dao.stream.apply/value` off a response that could only succeed.\n   195\t   A v2 response carries exactly one of `ok` or `error`, and correlation is\n   196\t   checked here rather than assumed from stream order.\"\n   197\t  [response call-id]\n   198\t  (when-not (apply2/response? response)\n   199\t    (throw (ex-info \"FFI response envelope is malformed\" {:response response})))\n   200\t  (when (and call-id (not= call-id (apply2/response-id response)))\n   201\t    (throw (ex-info \"FFI response does not correlate with this parked call\"\n   202\t                    {:call-id call-id,\n   203\t                     :response-id (apply2/response-id response)})))\n   204\t  (if-let [err (apply2/response-error response)]\n   205\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"FFI call failed: \"\n   206\t                         (:dao.stream.apply/message err))\n   207\t                    {:call-id call-id, :error err}))\n   208\t    (apply2/response-ok response)))\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\t(defn- apply-function\n   212\t  \"Shared logic for applying a function (primitive or closure) to arguments.\n   213\t   env is the active environment at the call site.\"\n   214\t  [state fn-value evaluated-operands k env]\n   215\t  (cond (fn? fn-value)\n   216\t        (handle-primitive-result state\n   217\t                                 (apply fn-value evaluated-operands)\n   218\t                                 k\n   219\t                                 env)\n   220\t        (= :closure (:type fn-value))\n   221\t        (let [{:keys [params body], closure-env :env} fn-value\n   222\t              extended-env (merge closure-env (zipmap params evaluated-operands))]\n   223\t          (cesk-return state body extended-env k (:value state)))\n   224\t        :else (throw (ex-info \"Cannot apply non-function\" {:fn fn-value}))))\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn- cesk-transition\n   228\t  \"Steps the CESK machine to evaluate an AST node.\n   229\t   Each return path produces exactly one ASTWalkerVM allocation via\n   230\t   cesk-return.\"\n   231\t  [state ast]\n   232\t  (let [{:keys [control env k store primitives modules]} state\n   233\t        {:keys [type], :as node} (or ast control)]\n   234\t    (if (and (nil? node) k)\n   235\t      (let [cont-type (:type k)]\n   236\t        (case cont-type\n   237\t          :eval-operator\n   238\t          (let [frame (:frame k)\n   239\t                fn-value (:value state)\n   240\t                operands (:operands frame)\n   241\t                saved-env (or (:env k) env)]\n   242\t            (if (empty? operands)\n   243\t              (apply-function state fn-value [] (:next k) saved-env)\n   244\t              (let [updated-frame (assoc frame\n   245\t                                         :operator-evaluated? true\n   246\t                                         :fn fn-value)]\n   247\t                (cesk-return state\n   248\t                             (first operands)\n   249\t                             saved-env\n   250\t                             (assoc k\n   251\t                                    :type :eval-operand\n   252\t                                    :frame updated-frame)\n   253\t                             nil))))\n   254\t          :eval-operand\n   255\t          (let [frame (:frame k)\n   256\t                operand-value (:value state)\n   257\t                evaluated (conj (or (:evaluated frame) []) operand-value)\n   258\t                operands (:operands frame)\n   259\t                saved-env (or (:env k) env)]\n   260\t            (if (= (count evaluated) (count operands))\n   261\t              (apply-function state (:fn frame) evaluated (:next k) saved-env)\n   262\t              (let [next-idx (count evaluated)\n   263\t                    next-node (nth operands next-idx)\n   264\t                    updated-frame (assoc frame :evaluated evaluated)]\n   265\t                (cesk-return state\n   266\t                             next-node\n   267\t                             saved-env\n   268\t                             (assoc k :frame updated-frame)\n   269\t                             nil))))\n   270\t          :eval-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
