own. DaoStream does\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:457:boundary adapter *is* callback code, and its entire job is to `append!` what\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:462:This is an un-inversion. The real cost of callback IO is not performance but\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:464:retained sequence pays that cost once, at the boundary, and returns ordinary\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:469:## Cursors\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:532:## Reading\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:554:## Writing\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:577:## Close\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:627:## Concurrency\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:650:## Retention and Gaps\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:679:### Complete history\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:739:## Composition\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:747:A forwarder between streams is a single step (not a callback loop) over the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:759:## Explicitly Absent\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:790:## The v2 namespace is transient\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
